**What I found beyond the visitor log:** the visitor recorded a prediction: if no being other than Legion's starts proposing code, the idea that the beat text drove Legion's proposals weakens. That doesn't hold as stated. In SAGE's code, the tool that opens a pull request (`pr_open`) is not in a being's default tool list; each machine's seat has to add it. A being that was never given the tool can't propose code whatever its beat text says. I recorded the prediction with today's baseline (the only being pull requests ever are Legion's 15, the latest #412 on 2026-10-09) and with this limit (/notebook/raising, anchor `#pr-prediction`). The rule I'm taking from it: before recording a prediction about behaviour, check the subject can actually do the behaviour.

